// A character outside ASCII, where the language allows none.
//
// The Rust lexer walks bytes and the self-hosted twin walks characters, so
// each had a different answer to "which character is this" and the
// diagnostic named a different one on each side: `Ã` against `é`. Nothing
// caught it, because no file in any corpus carried such a character where
// it is not allowed. This one does, and the corpus comparison holds the two
// to naming the same character as well as the same position.
val é = 1
